1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:27,420
Teddy!

3
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,820
Don't let your emotions get the better of you.

4
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,740
If you leave and I stay,

5
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,140
I'd never feel right about it.

6
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:35,580
I don't think you guys should leave.

7
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,500
But Coach will never forgive us.

8
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:40,490
What I wanted was to see you own up to
your mistakes with genuine remorse.

9
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:42,780
Is Class over!

10
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:44,220
The guillotine?

11
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:45,490
Who talks about guillotines at night?

12
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,580
When did I ever poke you?

13
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:51,420
Shawn, give it back.

14
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,780
You can pick it up from Coach Tony tomorrow.

15
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Episode 23

16
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:07,230
This is my Limited-Edition Yo-Yo.

17
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:08,850
The Ghost Face!

18
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:10,140
Ghost Face, Human Face... whatever.

19
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,540
Doesn't matter what Yo-Yo you use. Here I go!

20
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:13,950
Hold on!

21
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:15,900
You haven't announced the name of your Yo-Yo yet!

22
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:17,820
Who said I had to announce its name?

23
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:19,740
I think it adds a sense of proper ceremony.

24
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:23,100
A match should have a dignified procedure, okay?

25
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,060
Fine, fine.

26
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:25,760
My Yo-Yo's name is Shockwave. Here I go!

27
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,390
Wait, wait!

28
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,340
Wait for what? No more waiting! Here it goes!

29
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:47,100
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have brought
up something so painful for you.

30
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:52,380
Look at those 2 swans. They're so beautiful.

31
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:56,220
Aren't those just ducks?

32
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:59,580
You're the only person in the entire world

33
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,980
who can't tell the difference between a duck and a swan.

34
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:08,700
Coach!

35
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:13,020
Coach, we've got trouble!

36
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:13,950
What's wrong?

37
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:14,940
Matthew is challenging Shawn

38
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,380
to a Yo-Yo battle up in the tower!

39
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:19,260
That Matthew...

40
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,180
Shawn is terrified of heights!

41
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:23,100
Let's go.

42
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:00,060
Well? Think you can pull that off?

43
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:03,420
Why should I have to copy you?

44
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:05,340
Your moves are sloppy.

45
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,260
You've got no form, no style.

46
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,660
And you've got zero presence.

47
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:11,100
Oh, and also...

48
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:15,900
the transition between each move is just
a tiny bit off. It lacks flow.

49
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,580
This guy, Why do you always have so much to say?

50
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:20,020
There you go again.

51
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:22,140
You always just dismiss theory as pointless rambling.

52
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,440
That's the one and only thing
holding you back from true Mastery-

53
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:25,500
Enough!

54
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:27,390
Are you gonna do it or not?

55
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:29,310
Can you do it, or can't you?

56
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:31,740
What I do doesn't matter much. What you do matters a lot.

57
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:34,140
If I can't do it, it doesn't affect the big picture.

58
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:37,500
After all, my talent lies purely in the realm of theory.

59
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:39,870
But you, as a Professional Player,

60
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
if you can't do it right,

61
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:44,220
in the short term, it hurts the
whole Jianghai Team's performance.

62
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:48,030
And in the long term, it affects
the entire future of Yo-Yoing itself!

63
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,980
Alright, alright! I give up. You win.

64
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:52,350
I knew you'd come around to my way of thinking.

65
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:54,300
Hold on, let me finish.

66
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,000
What I'm saying is,

67
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,660
I'm not asking you to copy me anymore.

68
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:01,500
Just show me each of the Basic Moves, one by one,
And we'll call it your win.

69
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,900
Fine. I'll show you. Watch this:

70
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,600
"Reluctant to Part."

71
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:12,590
See? That is the standard, proper
form a true Yo-Yo player should have.

72
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:16,420
You drive me absolutely insane.

73
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,400
So what?

74
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,260
What's so great about that?

75
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,660
That "Reluctant to Part" thing you
just did is just a Beginner move.

76
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,440
It's child's play.

77
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:25,020
I'll call out an Advanced move. If you can pull it off,

78
00:05:25,660 --> 00:05:28,500
I'll admit you won. But if you can't,

79
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:32,300
then you never, ever teach us another class again.

80
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:36,510
How about we start with something Intermediate?

81
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:37,980
No more stalling. I'm done waiting for you.

82
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,420
Here's the deal. Do 10 Lightning Fast Strikes.

83
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:40,860
One move decides it all.

84
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,700
Looks like we'll be out of that class in no time.

85
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:46,620
You go first then.

86
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:48,990
Piece of cake.

87
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:49,980
Watch this!

88
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Your turn.

89
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,820
I'll show you! Lightning Fast Strike!

90
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,380
Ah! My Ghost Face!

91
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:19,740
My Limited-Edition Ghost Face!

92
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,540
You're gonna pay for that!

93
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,440
Pay? Pay for what?

94
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Shawn...

95
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:29,340
You've always been all talk and no action.

96
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:30,780
The only reason you're even on the Jianghai Team

97
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:32,220
is to be our errand boy.

98
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:35,100
And you actually think you're some kind of hotshot?

99
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,980
You... you've gone way too far!

100
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:39,900
That's a personal insult!

101
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:43,740
My Ghost Face!

102
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,940
Matthew, get down here right now!

103
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:03,900
Matthew, that was completely out of line!

104
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:07,740
How could you force Shawn into a match with you like that?

105
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,660
And then say those horrible things?

106
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:12,060
I just can't stand Shawn and his empty theories.

107
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,460
He can't even play, and yet he's so smug about it.

108
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,820
You have your strengths, and he has his.

109
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:21,660
Belittling him just because you're good at something else...
you think that's right?

110
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:24,540
But with Skills like his,

111
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,460
how is he supposed to teach us?

112
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:30,830
Having him teach you was my decision.
If you had a problem with it,

113
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,160
you should have come to me.

114
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:36,500
He was acting like his Authority was absolute,
and I just lost my temper.

115
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,660
Lost your temper over what?

116
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:41,340
I had Shawn teach you classes

117
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:44,220
so he could share his knowledge of Yo-Yos with all of you.

118
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:47,100
Because to master the Yo-Yo,

119
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,540
you can't just rely on raw Skill.

120
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,900
You have to understand its
History and the Principles behind it.

121
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:55,260
That's the only way you can really grow and innovate.

122
00:07:57,340 --> 00:07:59,100
Shawn's passion for Yo-Yos

123
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,980
is just as strong as anyone else on this Jianghai Team.

124
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,860
Sure, he can't play the Yo-Yo well himself.

125
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,780
But that's exactly why we should be helping him,

126
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,700
not mocking him for it.

127
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:12,060
And what's more,

128
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,460
he has contributed to this Jianghai Team greatly.

129
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,860
Even if he were just a regular Classmate,

130
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,780
how could you, knowing full well

131
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,700
that he's terrified of heights,

132
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:23,550
force him up a Tower for a Match?

133
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:25,500
Is that how a member of the Jianghai Team behaves?

134
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:28,860
Coach...

135
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,780
Coach!

136
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,540
Coach! Shawn... he ran off!

137
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,480
Where did he go?

138
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,120
We don't know.

139
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:42,300
All we found was this note he left behind.

140
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:43,710
The note said...

141
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:45,660
He's never gonna play Yo-Yo again.

142
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:49,020
Hurry, we have to find him!

143
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:58,140
Shawn! Come out!

144
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,030
Shawn, where are you?

145
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:05,000
Shawn!

146
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:30,300
Shawn!

147
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:32,220
Coach!

148
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:34,630
Anything? Not by the entrance either.

149
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:37,020
Looks like Shawn isn't in the Camp anymore.

150
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,420
I checked behind every single leaf.

151
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:41,020
You think Shawn's a cricket?

152
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,260
It's already dark out.

153
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,150
Our Camp is way out in the suburbs.

154
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:46,620
The last bus back to the City left ages ago.

155
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:50,460
It's dangerous for him to be wandering around at this hour.
We have to find him.

156
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,750
It's all my fault.

157
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:57,180
This isn't the time for blaming yourself. It's dark out.

158
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:02,940
Leo, you take everyone back to Camp.

159
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,400
I'll keep looking on my own.

160
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:07,260
Coach, there's strength in numbers.

161
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,630
We should all go together.

162
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:10,620
Yeah, Coach!

163
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:12,540
Alright, but you're all still young.

164
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,460
It's dangerous to be out at night.

165
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,970
Leo, take them back.

166
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:19,260
No one leaves without my permission.

167
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,180
Don't worry, Coach.

168
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:22,140
Be careful.

169
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:23,580
Here's a flashlight.

170
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,500
I'm off.

171
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:27,960
Take care out there, Coach!

172
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:21,660
Shawn!

173
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Shawn!

174
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:51,580
Shawn!

175
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:07,030
Excuse me, let me ask you something.

176
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:09,150
Have you seen a Student

177
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:11,580
about this tall wearing glasses?

178
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,500
I haven't seen any Students.

179
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:15,900
I did see someone picking through trash.

180
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,780
He was over that way.

181
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:21,180
Wearing glasses, right?

182
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:23,580
Glasses? Maybe, I didn't really notice.

183
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:25,980
Was it that way?

184
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:27,870
-Yeah, that way.
-Thank you, sir!

185
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:29,340
Thanks a lot!

186
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Shawn?

187
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:13,020
Shawn!

188
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:25,500
Coach!

189
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:29,340
Shawn!

190
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,420
Where have you been?

191
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,220
Don't eat that.

192
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:45,660
Coach!

193
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:48,540
Stop eating! That stuff's covered in pesticide!

194
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:54,780
Coach, I'm so hungry.

195
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:03,420
Alright, alright.

196
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:13,500
It's Ok, It's Ok.

197
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,420
I don't wanna leave you guys.

198
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:19,260
I know. I know.

199
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:25,020
No more tears.

200
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:30,300
Come on back. Everyone's waiting for you.

201
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:34,140
Enough crying. Come on, let's wipe your face.

202
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:39,900
No more crying. Let's go.

203
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,070
Shawn, slow down!

204
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:53,340
Don't choke.

205
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:58,620
Is that enough?

206
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:00,540
Yeah, that's plenty. Enough.

207
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,460
Shawn, if it's not enough, I've got more.

208
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:06,300
Oh man, Chuck, you've been holding out on us!

209
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:10,140
Where'd you get that? And why didn't you turn it in before?

210
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:12,060
I stashed it in a Secret spot

211
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:14,940
just in case I had a snack emergency.

212
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:17,790
You know, for when I just couldn't take it anymore.

213
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:20,220
Wow, you've got some nerve pulling a stunt like that.

214
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,590
But tell you what...

215
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,540
if you share the rest with everyone,

216
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:26,940
we won't hold you responsible.

217
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:29,820
But I don't have that much stashed away!

218
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:32,700
Shawn!

219
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,100
You're finally back.

220
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:40,380
I'm sorry, Shawn. I was wrong.

221
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:41,620
Shawn!

222
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:43,740
Matthew was so worried he didn't sleep a wink all night.

223
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,660
He's been out looking for you since early this morning.

224
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,540
It was my fault.

225
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:51,420
I swear to Coach Tony and to you, Shawn,

226
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:54,300
that from now on, I'll take theory seriously.

227
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,140
No more "All talk and no action."

228
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:02,430
Alright then. From now on, you 2 will help each other out.

229
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:04,380
You'll learn from each other.

230
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,450
No problem.

231
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:09,180
I'll take personal responsibility for helping Shawn practice.

232
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:12,540
But I've gotta say this up front:

233
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:16,860
no more practicing anywhere high up, got it?

234
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:30,870
Let's take a quick break!

235
00:16:31,420 --> 00:16:33,180
There's something I need to announce to everyone.

236
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:35,580
In 2 days,

237
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:37,980
our Training Camp here will be over and we'll be heading back.

238
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:40,830
So tomorrow, I've decided to give you all the day off.

239
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,300
You can pack up your own things,

240
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:43,740
and then in the evening,

241
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,110
we're going to hold a joint event with the Chengnan Team:

242
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:49,400
a Yo-Yo School Team Bonfire Party!

243
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:50,500
Sound good?

244
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:52,860
We get a day off!

245
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:53,820
Awesome!

246
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:57,150
What do you mean, "day off"? Summer break is over.

247
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,620
I meant we don't have to practice!

248
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:00,030
You don't wanna practice?

249
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:01,470
Then what kind of Jianghai Team member are you?

250
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:02,940
That's not what I meant!

251
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,380
What did you mean, then?

252
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,780
You're that happy just 'cause you don't have to practice?

253
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:09,660
Alright, alright, forget I even said anything.

254
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:13,470
The thing I'm looking forward to most right now

255
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:15,900
is grilling up all kinds of delicious stuff.

256
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:18,780
I really feel like belting out a song.

257
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:24,060
"Tomorrow, a touch of green..."

258
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:26,940
Should we put on a

259
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:28,830
fancy Yo-Yo performance?

260
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:29,820
Great idea!

261
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,710
We should probably rehearse the routine.

262
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:33,660
This is a chance to relax and have fun,

263
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:35,580
but it's also a chance to show our Team spirit.

264
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:36,800
Yeah!

265
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:55,260
Here they come!

266
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:07,260
Everyone, quiet down and listen up!

267
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:10,140
The joint Jianghai and Chengnan Team

268
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:13,980
